cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  The root metadata describe the unreleased post-v0.1.0 development tree.
  Cite the preferred manuscript record below for the mathematical results and
  the historical software reference below for the immutable v0.1.0
  software/source snapshot. Do not cite this development version as a released
  work.
title: "Two-sided computer-assisted progress on Erdős Problem 302"
type: software
version: "0.1.1-dev"
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Khanukov
    given-names: Dmitry
repository-code: "https://github.com/khanukov/erdos302"
url: "https://github.com/khanukov/erdos302"
abstract: >-
  Unreleased development materials following the preliminary, unrefereed
  v0.1.0 snapshot of two-sided partial progress on Erdős Problem 302. The
  latest archived version contains a qualitative Lean-checked lower
  improvement over density 5/8 and a computer-assisted exact upper bound; it
  has not been independently verified. Software and verification material are
  MIT-licensed; the manuscript is CC BY 4.0 under the path-specific scope in
  LICENSE_SCOPE.md. The v0.1.0 tag and DOI, rather than the moving default
  branch, define the latest published version.
keywords:
  - Erdős problems
  - extremal number theory
  - unit fractions
  - Lean 4
  - computer-assisted proof
